course: dictionary
lesson: 5695
title: Loess: the wind-blown soil
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about the world around us, and you learn them by reading about places. «Loess» is one of these. Read the words around it for clues: it is a soil, it is yellowish-brown, and it was carried by the wind.
explain: Here is the sentence: «China's Yellow River is named after the yellow-brown loess silt it carries, and that silt builds up in its bed, raising the river so it has changed its course many times, causing some of the deadliest floods in history.» The river is yellow-brown because of the loess it carries, so loess must be a yellow-brown soil.
explain: Loess is very fertile, which means it helps plants grow well, so farmers value it. But it wears away easily, so it can be washed or blown away. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: does «yellow-brown loess silt» still make sense? Yes, so you have understood it.
fact: Loess is a very fine, yellowish-brown soil.
fact: Loess is made of dust blown by the wind, often after the Ice Age.
fact: Loess makes very fertile farmland, but it wears away easily.
fact: The Loess Plateau in China is a famous place covered in loess.
fact: The Yellow River gets its colour from the loess it carries.
exercise: What colour is loess? | Bright blue | *Yellowish-brown | Jet black | Snow-white
exercise: Loess is made of what? | Old leaves from trees | *Dust blown by the wind | Sea water left behind on the sand | Melted rock from volcanoes
exercise: The Yellow River is yellow-brown because it carries what? | *Loess silt | Salt from the sea | Oil from ships | Ice from the mountains
test: Loess makes farmland that is very what? | Rocky | *Fertile | Empty | Cold
test: Loess wears away easily. What does wears away mean? | Stays exactly the same | Turns into stone | Grows bigger every year | *Gets worn down and carried off
exam: What is the best thing to do when you meet a new word like loess in a text? | Stop reading and give up | Guess a random colour | *Read the words around it to find clues to its meaning | Skip it completely and never think about it again
